  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "NVIDIA's NVFP4 (ModelOpt) quantization of Google Gemma 4 31B IT on one Spark with stock vLLM v0.25.1: 262144-token context, fp8 KV cache, up to 2 concurrent sequences, MTP speculative decoding (4 tokens) with Google's gemma-4-31B-it-assistant, image and video input, thinking on by default, Gemma 4 reasoning and tool-call parsers. Basis: MiaAI-Lab's start.sh (no licence file upstream; its README says scripts are MIT). Model and assistant are under Google's Gemma terms (recorded as information). Upstream throughput and KV-capacity figures are its claims; Vonk physical Spark acceptance is pending. Security note: upstream allows the server to fetch images from any URL (--allowed-media-domains *). Anyone who can send requests to this endpoint can make the Spark fetch arbitrary URLs, including addresses on your local network.",
    "tags": [
      "candidate",
